 "findings": [
  {
   "evidence": "`ChainRule/Higher.lean:52` fixes `{p : \u211d\u22650}` and `{\u03a9 : Opens \u2102}`, and `:85` states `contDiffOn_comp_succ` only at order `k + 1`. Every other planar API uses `p : \u211d\u22650\u221e` (`Basic.lean:296` `def MemWkpLoc (p : ENNReal) (U : Set \u2102)`, `ChainRule.lean:56`, `ChangeOfVariables/Higher.lean:74`). The wrapper's proof is only `lift p to \u211d\u22650 using hp'` plus `Nat.exists_eq_add_of_le'` followed by `contDiffOn_comp_succ`.",
   "file": "TauCeti/Geometry/Manifold/Sobolev/LocalMap/Atlas/Higher.lean",
   "fix": "Move it to `TauCeti/Analysis/Sobolev/Local/ChainRule/Higher.lean` as a public `MemWkpLoc.contDiffOn_comp_of_one_le` (or similar), with the `\u211d\u22650\u221e` exponent and an `IsOpen W` hypothesis. Import it here.",
   "issue": "`private MemWkpLoc.contDiffOn_comp_of_two_lt` is general planar infrastructure. It restates the every-order chain rule with `p : \u211d\u22650\u221e`, `p \u2260 \u22a4`, `1 \u2264 k` and a plain open `Set \u2102`. It uses only `MemWkpLoc`, `ContDiffOn` and `MapsTo`, with no manifold content, yet it is hidden in a manifold file. Callers of `MemWkpLoc.contDiffOn_comp_succ` in the usual `\u211d\u22650\u221e`/`Set` convention of the other planar lemmas have to redo the `lift p` and the `k = k' + 1` split.",
   "line": 107
  }
 ],
